{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792865670,"nonce":"Qo/p5xyFh//aOHj9In3udBuAqSo=","title":"An unsafe cast into a generic slot stores the source's bits, not a value of T","message":"In `class Test\u003cT:Float\u003e { var value:T; function fromFloat(v:Float) this.value = cast v; function get():T return value; }`, the erased body lowers `cast v` as `bitcast f64 -\u003e i64`. The `Test\u003cInt\u003e` specialisation keeps that bitcast, so `fromFloat(12)` stores 0x4028000000000000 and `get__i32` reads its low word: 0.\n\nReproducer: conformance Issue2835's shape as a standalone file, run with `RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES=inlining --tier-start-interpreted false` -\u003e `42 0 \u003cgarbage\u003e` instead of `42 12 12`. With inlining the constant folder happens to produce 12, which is why native and the O0 interpreter start pass.\n\nFix direction: lower a cast to a type parameter as a cast to `TypeVar(T)` so monomorphisation turns it into a numeric conversion for a scalar T, and a bit copy only for the erased body.","files":null}]}